aration order for the compiler is assumed, as IDSCH is␀1766| 5  ;  passed only ^symcursor.␀1766| 5  ;    symcursor: cursrange (* index into symbufarray *);␀1766| 5  ;    sy: symbol (* symbol = (ident..othersy), set by info in reswrdtable *);␀1766| 5  ;    op: operator (* more info from reswrdtable *);␀1766| 5  ;    id: alfa (* packed array [1..8] of char, gets filled with first 8 chars␀1766| 5  ;          of token isolated by IDSRCH if token is an identifier *);␀1766| 5  ␀1766| 5  ; Isolate token, converting to upper case.␀1766| 5  ; If token in reswrdtable set sy and op from table,␀1766| 5  ; else set st := ident, and put first 8 chars (left-justified) of␀1766| 5  ;   token into id.␀1766| 5  ; symcursor is left pointing to the last char of the token␀1766| 5  ␀1766| 0290 0  SYMCUR  .EQU    WORD1           ; index into symbufarray␀1766| 0292 0  SYMBUFP .EQU    WORD2           ; ^symcursarray␀1766| 0294 0  RESWRDP .EQU    WORD3           ; ^reswrdtable␀1766| 0296 0  IDEND   .EQU    WORD4           ; loop control␀1766| 0298 0  TOKEN   .EQU    BLOCK1          ; first 8 chars of isolated token goes here␀1766| 5  ␀1766| 5  RESTBL  ; reswrdtable␀1766| 5 (; TYPE table = RECORD␀1766| 5 (;                indexes: ARRAY ['A'..succ('Z')] OF integer;␀1766| 5 (;                tokens: ARRAY [0..#] OF RECORD␀1766| 5 (;                          tokenname: alfa;␀1766| 5 (;                          tokentype: symbol;␀1766| 5 (;                          optype: operator␀1766| 5 (;                        END␀1766| 5 (;              END;␀1766| 5  ; Index part␀1766| 0000 0200 0300 0500   (.WORD   0,  2,  3,  5,  8, 11., 15., 16., 16.␀176E| 0800 0B00 0F00 1000   1776| 1000 0 1778| 1400 1400 1400 1500   (.WORD  20., 20., 20., 21., 22., 23., 25., 28., 28.␀1780| 1600 1700 1900 1C00   1788| 1C00 0 178A| 1E00 2100 2400 2700   (.WORD  30., 33., 36., 39., 40., 42., 42., 42., 42.␀1792| 2800 2A00 2A